## 6. FAILED-MODEL RETRY BEHAVIOR

This section is especially important.

Preserve the existing retry strategy:

1. Ordinary models are tested first.
2. Failed ordinary models are retried only after all enabled ordinary providers have no untested models.
3. Confirmed models must not be treated as ordinary failed models.
4. When starting a retry round, reset the appropriate failed ordinary models to `untested`.
5. Preserve the existing round-number and round-count updates.
6. Preserve the existing recursive or equivalent selection flow, provided it remains safe.

Because the provider list is now dynamic, the exhaustion check must consider only enabled providers.

Likewise, the failed-model retry set must not reintroduce ordinary models belonging to disabled providers.

Do not change retry timing or the fundamental retry policy.

